    "notes": {
        "94e2fbdc-8950-4711-89e2-50e0749a4fd4": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 64,
            "width": 560,
            "height": 220,
            "content": "## Test data assumption\n\n- Account: a **Telegram User** account (service `appmixer:telegram:user`) — API ID, API Hash and a session string of a **user** (not bot) account.\n- Reads the official public channel **@telegram** without joining it. It always has posts, so FindChannelMessages (`First Item Only`) never hits `notFound`.\n- Read-only: nothing is created, so there is no cleanup step.\n- If @telegram is restricted in the account's region, point both components at another public channel and update the asserted channel username/URL on Find Channel Messages."
        }
    }
